docs {
  ## API explanation
  **Booking step 2.** The flow is: 1. choose package -> 2. choose teacher ->
  3. fill in details and pay. This is what step 2 renders.

  Given a package, it returns the teachers that package can be booked with, each
  carrying their full bookable slot list for the requested window -- so step 2
  and the date picker are one screen with no follow-up call per teacher.

  **Which teachers come back.** A package with no teachers assigned is
  unrestricted and offers every active teacher (the default, and what all four
  seeded packages do). Assign teachers via
  `PATCH /administrator/packages/<id>/ {"teachers": ["<uuid>", ...]}` to limit it.
  `package.restricted` tells you which case you are in.

  A teacher with **zero** bookable slots in the window is omitted entirely --
  picking them would lead to an empty calendar. If a restricted package's only
  teachers are all deactivated, it falls back to every active teacher rather than
  showing an empty picker.

  Query params:

  - `date` -- `YYYY-MM-DD`, first day of the window. Defaults to today (school time).
  - `days` -- 1-31, defaults to 7.
  - `tz` -- IANA name, defaults to `America/Guayaquil`. An unknown zone returns 400.
  - `lang` -- `en` or `es`, applies to the package title and teacher bios.

  `days` always contains one entry per requested day, including empty weekends,
  so a week grid renders without gaps. `next_available` is the first slot across
  the whole window, ready for a "Next available: Mon 14:00" badge.
  `slot_count` is the total across the window.

  Post the chosen `start_utc` verbatim to **checkout** as `start_datetime`.

  The restriction is enforced again at checkout and when a student books a later
  class from the portal -- filtering this list is not the only guard.

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "package": {
      "id": "347cde65-90ad-4178-8816-332e19e04748",
      "title": "10-Class Package",
      "price": "135.00",
      "total_classes": 10,
      "is_first_lesson": false,
      "restricted": false
    },
    "timezone": "Europe/London",
    "duration_minutes": 60,
    "from_date": "2026-09-07",
    "days_requested": 7,
    "teachers": [
      {
        "id": "1e54776b-9910-4742-9f8c-8efd23912d4a",
        "name": "Fernando Cordero",
        "profile_img_url": "",
        "tags": ["beginners", "conversation", "travel spanish"],
        "institute": "Universidad Central del Ecuador",
        "availability": [{ "day": "mon", "start": "08:00", "end": "16:00" }],
        "accepting_students": true,
        "availability_label": "Accepting new students",
        "description": "I have taught Spanish for twelve years...",
        "lang": "en",
        "next_available": {
          "start_utc": "2026-09-07T13:00:00+00:00",
          "start_local": "2026-09-07T14:00:00+01:00",
          "label": "14:00",
          "date": "2026-09-07"
        },
        "slot_count": 40,
        "days": [
          {
            "date": "2026-09-07",
            "slots": [
              {
                "start_utc": "2026-09-07T13:00:00+00:00",
                "start_local": "2026-09-07T14:00:00+01:00",
                "label": "14:00"
              }
            ]
          },
          { "date": "2026-09-12", "slots": [] }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
